     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\":4,\"rationale\":\"At least 4 blocks are needed, and 4 are enough.\\n\\nWhy 4 is enough: blocking dbReplica:collection, codeRepo:collection, shareMount:collection and mailArchive:collection removes every parent of the OR target crownData:exfiltrate.\\n\\nWhy fewer will not do: there are four routes to the target, and no single blockable step lies on more than one of them, so each route needs its own block.\\n1) phishing -> browserStore -> fileServer -> mailArchive -> target. All of these are OR steps.\\n2) wifiGuest -> sshKey -> jumpHost -> shareMount -> target. All OR steps.\\n3) wifiGuest -> kerberoast -> backupHost -> codeRepo -> target. All OR steps.\\n4) workstation + containerHost -> vpnSession (AND) -> monitoringHost -> dbReplica -> target. This route can be broken by blocking workstation, containerHost, vpnSession, monitoringHost or dbReplica.\\n\\nThe blockable steps of each route (routes 1-3: browserStore, fileServer, mailArchive / sshKey, jumpHost, shareMount / kerberoast, backupHost, codeRepo) never appear in another route. So any blocking set must contain at least four distinct steps.\"}"
    }
   ],
